hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23307","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, that Ibn Buhayna informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood in the two rak'as of Zuhr, forgetting the sitting, until when he finished his prayer before giving salam, he prostrated two prostrations, then ended with the taslim."
"23308","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Ibn Buhayna: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in a prayer we think it was Asr, and he stood in the second and did not sit, then when it was before giving salam, he prostrated two prostrations."
"23309","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: And Shu'ba narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Hafs ibn Asim narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Malik Ibn Buhayna, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man praying the two rak'as of Fajr while the prayer had been established, then when he finished the prayer, the people crowded around him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-Subh four."
"23310","Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz informed me, from Abd Allah Ibn Buhayna, and he was of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did any of you recite with me just now. They said: Yes. He said: I say, what is with me that I am contended with over the Qur'an. So the people stopped reciting with him when he said that."
"23311","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rashdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'a, from Ibn Hurmuz, from Ibn Buhayna, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prostrated, spread his arms in his prostration until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"23312","Abu Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama, that he heard Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Buhayna say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped at Lahy Jamal on the road from Makka, on the middle of his head, while he was in ihram."
"23313","Qutayba ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'a, from al-A'raj, from Abd Allah ibn Malik Ibn Buhayna, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed, separated his hands until the whiteness of his armpits appeared."
"23314","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, Hafs ibn Asim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Malik Ibn Buhayna, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man while the iqama for prayer had been made and he was praying the two rak'as before Fajr, so he said to him something we do not know what it was, then when we finished, we surrounded him saying: What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say to you. He said: He said to me: One of you is about to pray al-Subh four."
"23315","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abd Allah ibn Malik Ibn Buhayna, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by him while he was praying, prolonging his prayer or something like this, before the Fajr prayer, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Do not make this like the Zuhr prayer, before it and after it; make a separation between them."
"23316","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, and Hajjaj, Shu'ba informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Hafs ibn Asim and others, Hajjaj said in his hadith, he said: I heard Hafs ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Malik Ibn Buhayna, that a man entered the mosque while the prayer had been established, and he prayed the two rak'as of Fajr, then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, the people crowded around him, so he said: Al-Subh four."
"23317","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abd Allah Ibn Buhayna, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for us two rak'as, then stood and did not sit, so the people stood with him, then when he finished his prayer and we awaited his taslim, he said takbir and prostrated two prostrations while sitting before the taslim, then gave salam."
"23318","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj informed him, from Abd Allah Ibn Buhayna, and he was of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for them two rak'as, then stood and did not sit in them, so the people stood with him, then when he prayed the other two rak'as, the people awaited his taslim, so he said takbir and prostrated, then said takbir and prostrated, then gave salam."
"23319","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me also, from Ibn Buhayna al-Asadi, and Ibn Bakr said: al-Azdi, the ally of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood in Zuhr while sitting was due upon him, then when he completed his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting before giving salam, saying takbir in every prostration, and the people prostrated with him in place of what he forgot of sitting."
"23320","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj, the mawla of Rabi'a ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, informed him, that he heard Abd Allah Ibn Buhayna al-Azdi, Azd Shanu'a, and he is the ally of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for us two rak'as, then stood and did not sit after the two rak'as, so the people stood with him, then when he finished his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting before the taslim, then gave salam."
"23321","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abd Allah Ibn Buhayna, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood in the first two rak'as of Zuhr or Asr and did not sit, then when he finished his prayer, he said: He prostrated two prostrations before giving salam."
"23322","Abd Allah said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Malik Ibn Buhayna, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out for the Subh prayer while Ibn al-Qishb was praying, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck his shoulder and said: O Ibn al-Qishb, do you pray al-Subh four. Or twice, Ibn Jurayj doubts."
